## [FailurePolicy - Failure policy]($heading.id('failurepolicy---failure-policy'))


A timeout or a finding outside the inherited baseline is a new failure.
The inherited policy determines whether existing findings also guard an action.

### [FailurePolicy - NewFailure]($heading.id('failurepolicy---newfailure'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{NewFailure} ( \mathit{failures} , \mathit{baseline} ) \triangleq \texttt{"timeout"} \in \mathit{failures} \lor \neg ( \mathit{failures} \subseteq \mathit{baseline} )
\end{aligned}
```

### [FailurePolicy - FailureGuards]($heading.id('failurepolicy---failureguards'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{FailureGuards} ( \mathit{failures} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{inherited} ) \triangleq \mathit{failures} \neq \{ \} \land ( \mathit{inherited} = \texttt{"block"} \lor \mathit{NewFailure} ( \mathit{failures} , \mathit{baseline} ) )
\end{aligned}
```

# [Overwatch]($heading.id('overwatch'))

[Source](https://github.com/benomahony/overwatch/blob/main/spec/Overwatch.tla)

## [Overwatch - Imports]($heading.id('overwatch---imports'))


Shared operators used by this module are imported below.

### [Overwatch - EXTENDS]($heading.id('overwatch---extends'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{EXTENDS} \mathit{Naturals} , \mathit{FiniteSets} , \mathit{Sequences} , \mathit{FailurePolicy}
\end{aligned}
```

## [Overwatch - State and result domains]($heading.id('overwatch---state-and-result-domains'))


Workspace versions, completed outcomes, and message records form the result layer.
Finite bounds are supplied by the TLC configuration, not by the runtime.

### [Overwatch - CONSTANTS]($heading.id('overwatch---constants'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{CONSTANTS} \mathit{Names} , \mathit{MaxEdits} , \mathit{Timeout}
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - ASSUME]($heading.id('overwatch---assume'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{ASSUME} \texttt{"timeout"} \notin \mathit{Names}
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - Versions]($heading.id('overwatch---versions'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Versions} \triangleq 0 \mathbin{\text{..}} \mathit{MaxEdits}
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - Results]($heading.id('overwatch---results'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Results} \triangleq \mathit{SUBSET} \mathit{Names}
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - TimedOut]($heading.id('overwatch---timedout'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{TimedOut} \triangleq \texttt{"timeout"}
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - Outcomes]($heading.id('overwatch---outcomes'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Outcomes} \triangleq \mathit{SUBSET} ( \mathit{Names} \cup \{ \mathit{TimedOut} \} )
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - NoMessage]($heading.id('overwatch---nomessage'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{NoMessage} \triangleq [ \mathit{held} \mapsto \mathit{FALSE} , \mathit{waking} \mapsto \mathit{FALSE} , \mathit{failures} \mapsto \{ \} ]
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - NotTold]($heading.id('overwatch---nottold'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{NotTold} \triangleq [ \mathit{kind} \mapsto \texttt{"none"} , \mathit{fresh} \mapsto \{ \} ]
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - NoBaseline]($heading.id('overwatch---nobaseline'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{NoBaseline} \triangleq [ \mathit{known} \mapsto \mathit{FALSE} , \mathit{at} \mapsto 0 , \mathit{failures} \mapsto \{ \} ]
\end{aligned}
```

## [Overwatch - State shape]($heading.id('overwatch---state-shape'))


The checked version, unread results, inherited baseline, and delivery state are
separate. touched records whether the session has edited since the commit the
baseline belongs to; own is the versions those edits made, which only the
properties read. TypeOK constrains their domains without advancing an execution.

### [Overwatch - VARIABLES]($heading.id('overwatch---variables'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{VARIABLES} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\mathit{truth} , \mathit{head} , \mathit{based} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{from} , \mathit{quiet} , \mathit{installed} , \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\mathit{produced} , \mathit{consumed} , \mathit{pending} , \mathit{report} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{wasFailing} , \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\mathit{outbox} , \mathit{told} , \mathit{flush} , \mathit{turn} , \mathit{toldThisTurn} , \mathit{promptQueued} , \mathit{knows} , \mathit{elapsed} , \mathit{edited} , \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\mathit{touched} , \mathit{own}
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - vars]($heading.id('overwatch---vars'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{vars} \triangleq \langle \mathit{truth} , \mathit{head} , \mathit{based} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{from} , \mathit{quiet} , \mathit{installed} , \\
&\quad \hspace{3.33em}\mathit{produced} , \mathit{consumed} , \mathit{pending} , \mathit{report} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{wasFailing} , \\
&\quad \hspace{3.33em}\mathit{outbox} , \mathit{told} , \mathit{flush} , \mathit{turn} , \mathit{toldThisTurn} , \mathit{promptQueued} , \mathit{knows} , \mathit{elapsed} , \mathit{edited} , \\
&\quad \hspace{3.33em}\mathit{touched} , \mathit{own} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - TypeOK]($heading.id('overwatch---typeok'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{TypeOK} \triangleq \land \mathit{truth} \in [ \mathit{Versions} \to \mathit{Results} ] \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{head} \in \mathit{Versions} \land \mathit{based} \in 0 \mathbin{\text{..}} \mathit{head} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{busy} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \land \mathit{from} \in \mathit{Versions} \land \mathit{quiet} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \land \mathit{installed} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{produced} \in 0 \mathbin{\text{..}} ( \mathit{MaxEdits} + 1 ) \land \mathit{consumed} \in 0 \mathbin{\text{..}} \mathit{produced} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{pending} \in \mathit{Seq} ( [ \mathit{id} : 1 \mathbin{\text{..}} ( \mathit{MaxEdits} + 1 ) , \mathit{at} : \mathit{Versions} , \mathit{failures} : \mathit{Outcomes} ] ) \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{Len} ( \mathit{pending} ) \leq \mathit{MaxEdits} + 1 \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{report} \in [ \mathit{known} : \mathit{BOOLEAN} , \mathit{id} : 0 \mathbin{\text{..}} \mathit{produced} , \mathit{at} : \mathit{Versions} , \mathit{failures} : \mathit{Outcomes} ] \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{baseline} \in [ \mathit{known} : \mathit{BOOLEAN} , \mathit{at} : \mathit{Versions} , \mathit{failures} : \mathit{Outcomes} ] \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{wasFailing} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{outbox} \in [ \mathit{held} : \mathit{BOOLEAN} , \mathit{waking} : \mathit{BOOLEAN} , \mathit{failures} : \mathit{Outcomes} ] \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{told} \in [ \mathit{kind} : \{ \texttt{"none"} , \texttt{"failed"} , \texttt{"recovered"} \} , \mathit{fresh} : \mathit{Outcomes} ] \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{flush} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{turn} \in \{ \texttt{"idle"} , \texttt{"running"} \} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{toldThisTurn} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \land \mathit{promptQueued} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{knows} \in \mathit{Outcomes} \land \mathit{elapsed} \in 0 \mathbin{\text{..}} \mathit{Timeout} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{edited} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{touched} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \land \mathit{own} \subseteq \mathit{Versions}
\end{aligned}
```

## [Overwatch - Failure gating]($heading.id('overwatch---failure-gating'))


A failure report becomes a gate only when it is a regression against the
session baseline, or when the check times out.

### [Overwatch - Failing]($heading.id('overwatch---failing'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Failing} \triangleq \mathit{report} . \mathit{known} \land \mathit{report} . \mathit{failures} \neq \{ \}
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - Regressed]($heading.id('overwatch---regressed'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Regressed} ( \mathit{f} ) \triangleq \mathit{TimedOut} \in \mathit{f} \lor ( \mathit{baseline} . \mathit{known} \land \mathit{NewFailure} ( \mathit{f} , \mathit{baseline} . \mathit{failures} ) )
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - Guard]($heading.id('overwatch---guard'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Guard} \triangleq \mathit{Failing} \land \mathit{Regressed} ( \mathit{report} . \mathit{failures} )
\end{aligned}
```

## [Overwatch - Initial state]($heading.id('overwatch---initial-state'))


The first check starts at the inherited workspace version. No result or
baseline is known and no notification has been sent.

### [Overwatch - Init]($heading.id('overwatch---init'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Init} \triangleq \land \mathit{truth} \in [ \mathit{Versions} \to \mathit{Results} ] \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{head} = 0 \land \mathit{based} = 0 \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{busy} = \mathit{TRUE} \land \mathit{from} = 0 \land \mathit{quiet} = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{installed} = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{produced} = 0 \land \mathit{consumed} = 0 \land \mathit{pending} = \langle \rangle \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{report} = [ \mathit{known} \mapsto \mathit{FALSE} , \mathit{id} \mapsto 0 , \mathit{at} \mapsto 0 , \mathit{failures} \mapsto \{ \} ] \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{baseline} = \mathit{NoBaseline} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{wasFailing} = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{outbox} = \mathit{NoMessage} \land \mathit{told} = \mathit{NotTold} \land \mathit{flush} = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{turn} = \texttt{"idle"} \land \mathit{toldThisTurn} = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{promptQueued} = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{knows} = \{ \} \land \mathit{elapsed} = 0 \land \mathit{edited} = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{touched} = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{own} = \{ \}
\end{aligned}
```

## [Overwatch - Result delivery and baseline isolation]($heading.id('overwatch---result-delivery-and-baseline-isolation'))


Queue deduplicates notification signatures. Deliver consumes a completed
snapshot, establishes the inherited baseline, and queues a regression or recovery.
The first result is the baseline unless the session has edited since the
commit, as another process's changes are inherited like the commit itself; after
a session edit the baseline is empty, so no failure the edit may hold is absorbed.
A recovery can cancel a failure message that has not yet been delivered.

### [Overwatch - Queue]($heading.id('overwatch---queue'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Queue} ( \mathit{signature} , \mathit{message} ) \triangleq \mathit{IF} \mathit{told} = \mathit{signature} \land \neg \mathit{outbox} . \mathit{held} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\mathit{THEN} \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{outbox} , \mathit{told} , \mathit{flush} \rangle \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\mathit{ELSE} \land \mathit{told} ' = \mathit{signature} \land \mathit{outbox} ' = \mathit{message} \land \mathit{flush} ' = \mathit{TRUE}
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - Deliver]($heading.id('overwatch---deliver'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Deliver} ( \mathit{v} , \mathit{id} , \mathit{f} ) \triangleq \mathit{LET} \mathit{b} \triangleq \mathit{IF} \mathit{baseline} . \mathit{known} \mathit{THEN} \mathit{baseline} . \mathit{failures} \mathit{ELSE} \mathit{IF} \neg \mathit{touched} \mathit{THEN} \mathit{f} \mathit{ELSE} \{ \} \\
&\quad \hspace{2.67em}\mathit{isRegression} \triangleq \mathit{TimedOut} \in \mathit{f} \lor \neg ( \mathit{f} \subseteq \mathit{b} ) \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\mathit{IN} \land \mathit{report} ' = [ \mathit{known} \mapsto \mathit{TRUE} , \mathit{id} \mapsto \mathit{id} , \mathit{at} \mapsto \mathit{v} , \mathit{failures} \mapsto \mathit{f} ] \\
&\quad \hspace{2.33em}\land \mathit{baseline} ' = \mathit{IF} \mathit{TimedOut} \in \mathit{f} \lor \mathit{baseline} . \mathit{known} \mathit{THEN} \mathit{baseline} \\
&\quad \hspace{7.33em}\mathit{ELSE} [ \mathit{known} \mapsto \mathit{TRUE} , \mathit{at} \mapsto \mathit{v} , \mathit{failures} \mapsto \mathit{b} ] \\
&\quad \hspace{2.33em}\land \mathit{wasFailing} ' = \mathit{isRegression} \\
&\quad \hspace{2.33em}\land \mathit{IF} \mathit{isRegression} \\
&\quad \hspace{4.0em}\mathit{THEN} \mathit{Queue} ( [ \mathit{kind} \mapsto \texttt{"failed"} , \mathit{fresh} \mapsto \mathit{f} \setminus \mathit{b} ] , \\
&\quad \hspace{7.67em}[ \mathit{held} \mapsto \mathit{TRUE} , \mathit{waking} \mapsto \mathit{edited} \lor \mathit{TimedOut} \in \mathit{f} , \mathit{failures} \mapsto \mathit{f} ] ) \\
&\quad \hspace{3.33em}\mathit{ELSE} \mathit{IF} \neg \mathit{wasFailing} \\
&\quad \hspace{4.0em}\mathit{THEN} \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{outbox} , \mathit{told} , \mathit{flush} \rangle \\
&\quad \hspace{3.33em}\mathit{ELSE} \mathit{IF} \mathit{outbox} . \mathit{held} \\
&\quad \hspace{4.0em}\mathit{THEN} \land \mathit{outbox} ' = \mathit{NoMessage} \land \mathit{told} ' = \mathit{NotTold} \land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \mathit{flush} \\
&\quad \hspace{3.33em}\mathit{ELSE} \mathit{Queue} ( [ \mathit{kind} \mapsto \texttt{"recovered"} , \mathit{fresh} \mapsto \{ \} ] , [ \mathit{held} \mapsto \mathit{TRUE} , \mathit{waking} \mapsto \mathit{FALSE} , \mathit{failures} \mapsto \mathit{f} ] )
\end{aligned}
```

## [Overwatch - Workspace changes and scheduling]($heading.id('overwatch---workspace-changes-and-scheduling'))


An agent edit advances head without moving based, and marks the next read as
following the agent's own change and the session as having edited. Another
process can change the workspace at any time without committing; OutsideEdit
advances head the same way but marks nothing. An external head change moves both,
invalidates the baseline and unread results, and starts the session's edits
afresh. QuietElapses starts the next check; Tick advances its timeout clock.

### [Overwatch - Edit]($heading.id('overwatch---edit'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Edit} \triangleq \land \mathit{turn} = \texttt{"running"} \land \mathit{head} < \mathit{MaxEdits} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{head} ' = \mathit{head} + 1 \land \mathit{quiet} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \land \mathit{edited} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{touched} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \land \mathit{own} ' = \mathit{own} \cup \{ \mathit{head} + 1 \} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{truth} , \mathit{based} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{from} , \mathit{installed} , \mathit{produced} , \mathit{consumed} , \mathit{pending} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{report} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{wasFailing} , \mathit{outbox} , \mathit{told} , \mathit{flush} , \mathit{turn} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{toldThisTurn} , \mathit{promptQueued} , \mathit{knows} , \mathit{elapsed} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - OutsideEdit]($heading.id('overwatch---outsideedit'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{OutsideEdit} \triangleq \land \mathit{head} < \mathit{MaxEdits} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{head} ' = \mathit{head} + 1 \land \mathit{quiet} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{truth} , \mathit{based} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{from} , \mathit{installed} , \mathit{produced} , \mathit{consumed} , \mathit{pending} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{report} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{wasFailing} , \mathit{outbox} , \mathit{told} , \mathit{flush} , \mathit{turn} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{toldThisTurn} , \mathit{promptQueued} , \mathit{knows} , \mathit{elapsed} , \mathit{edited} , \mathit{touched} , \mathit{own} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - HeadMoves]($heading.id('overwatch---headmoves'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{HeadMoves} \triangleq \land \mathit{head} < \mathit{MaxEdits} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{head} ' = \mathit{head} + 1 \land \mathit{based} ' = \mathit{head} + 1 \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{baseline} ' = \mathit{NoBaseline} \land \mathit{touched} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{own} ' = \{ \} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{quiet} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \land \mathit{pending} ' = \langle \rangle \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{from} ' = \mathit{IF} \mathit{busy} \mathit{THEN} \mathit{head} + 1 \mathit{ELSE} \mathit{from} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{elapsed} ' = \mathit{IF} \mathit{busy} \mathit{THEN} 0 \mathit{ELSE} \mathit{elapsed} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{truth} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{installed} , \mathit{produced} , \mathit{consumed} , \mathit{report} , \mathit{wasFailing} , \mathit{outbox} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{told} , \mathit{flush} , \mathit{turn} , \mathit{toldThisTurn} , \mathit{promptQueued} , \mathit{knows} , \mathit{edited} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - QuietElapses]($heading.id('overwatch---quietelapses'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{QuietElapses} \triangleq \land \mathit{quiet} \land \mathit{installed} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{quiet} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{busy} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \land \mathit{from} ' = \mathit{head} \land \mathit{elapsed} ' = 0 \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{truth} , \mathit{head} , \mathit{based} , \mathit{installed} , \mathit{produced} , \mathit{consumed} , \mathit{pending} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{report} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{wasFailing} , \mathit{outbox} , \mathit{told} , \mathit{flush} , \mathit{turn} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{toldThisTurn} , \mathit{promptQueued} , \mathit{knows} , \mathit{edited} , \mathit{touched} , \mathit{own} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - Tick]($heading.id('overwatch---tick'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Tick} \triangleq \land \mathit{busy} \land \mathit{elapsed} < \mathit{Timeout} \land \mathit{elapsed} ' = \mathit{elapsed} + 1 \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{truth} , \mathit{head} , \mathit{based} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{from} , \mathit{quiet} , \mathit{installed} , \mathit{produced} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{consumed} , \mathit{pending} , \mathit{report} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{wasFailing} , \mathit{outbox} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{told} , \mathit{flush} , \mathit{turn} , \mathit{toldThisTurn} , \mathit{promptQueued} , \mathit{knows} , \mathit{edited} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{touched} , \mathit{own} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

Completion appends a result; it does not deliver it. Partial output is a    stuttering step at this abstraction: only a complete build enters pending.

## [Overwatch - Buffered completion and consumption]($heading.id('overwatch---buffered-completion-and-consumption'))


Run completion appends a snapshot to pending without publishing it.
ReadResults consumes the newest completed snapshot and clears the buffer.
A later incomplete build does not replace an earlier complete result.

### [Overwatch - Buffer]($heading.id('overwatch---buffer'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Buffer} ( \mathit{v} , \mathit{f} ) \triangleq \land \mathit{produced} ' = \mathit{produced} + 1 \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{pending} ' = \mathit{Append} ( \mathit{pending} , [ \mathit{id} \mapsto \mathit{produced} + 1 , \mathit{at} \mapsto \mathit{v} , \mathit{failures} \mapsto \mathit{f} ] ) \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{busy} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{installed} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{truth} , \mathit{head} , \mathit{based} , \mathit{from} , \mathit{quiet} , \mathit{consumed} , \mathit{report} , \mathit{baseline} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{wasFailing} , \mathit{outbox} , \mathit{told} , \mathit{flush} , \mathit{turn} , \mathit{toldThisTurn} , \mathit{promptQueued} , \mathit{knows} , \mathit{elapsed} , \mathit{edited} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{touched} , \mathit{own} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - RunEnds]($heading.id('overwatch---runends'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{RunEnds} \triangleq \mathit{busy} \land \exists \mathit{v} \in \mathit{from} \mathbin{\text{..}} \mathit{head} : \mathit{Buffer} ( \mathit{v} , \mathit{truth} [ \mathit{v} ] )
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - TimesOut]($heading.id('overwatch---timesout'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{TimesOut} \triangleq \mathit{busy} \land \mathit{elapsed} = \mathit{Timeout} \land \mathit{Buffer} ( \mathit{from} , \{ \mathit{TimedOut} \} )
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - ReadResults]($heading.id('overwatch---readresults'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{ReadResults} \triangleq \land \mathit{pending} \neq \langle \rangle \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{LET} \mathit{latest} \triangleq \mathit{pending} [ \mathit{Len} ( \mathit{pending} ) ] \\
&\quad \hspace{2.33em}\mathit{IN} \mathit{Deliver} ( \mathit{latest} . \mathit{at} , \mathit{latest} . \mathit{id} , \mathit{latest} . \mathit{failures} ) \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{consumed} ' = \mathit{produced} \land \mathit{pending} ' = \langle \rangle \land \mathit{edited} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{truth} , \mathit{head} , \mathit{based} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{from} , \mathit{quiet} , \mathit{installed} , \mathit{produced} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{turn} , \mathit{toldThisTurn} , \mathit{promptQueued} , \mathit{knows} , \mathit{elapsed} , \mathit{touched} , \mathit{own} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

## [Overwatch - Notification delivery and turn completion]($heading.id('overwatch---notification-delivery-and-turn-completion'))


A running turn receives at most one notification before another turn starts.
An idle agent can receive one queued wakeup. Flush publishes eligible messages;
TurnCompletes keeps a guarded turn running and permits a clean turn to settle.

### [Overwatch - Held]($heading.id('overwatch---held'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Held} \triangleq \mathit{IF} \mathit{turn} = \texttt{"running"} \mathit{THEN} \mathit{toldThisTurn} \mathit{ELSE} \mathit{promptQueued} \lor \neg \mathit{outbox} . \mathit{waking}
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - Flush]($heading.id('overwatch---flush'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Flush} \triangleq \land \mathit{flush} \land \mathit{flush} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{IF} \mathit{outbox} . \mathit{held} \land \neg \mathit{Held} \\
&\quad \hspace{3.0em}\mathit{THEN} \land \mathit{outbox} ' = \mathit{NoMessage} \land \mathit{knows} ' = \mathit{outbox} . \mathit{failures} \\
&\quad \hspace{4.67em}\land \mathit{IF} \mathit{turn} = \texttt{"running"} \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{THEN} \mathit{toldThisTurn} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \mathit{promptQueued} \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{ELSE} \mathit{promptQueued} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \mathit{toldThisTurn} \\
&\quad \hspace{3.0em}\mathit{ELSE} \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{outbox} , \mathit{knows} , \mathit{toldThisTurn} , \mathit{promptQueued} \rangle \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{truth} , \mathit{head} , \mathit{based} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{from} , \mathit{quiet} , \mathit{installed} , \mathit{produced} , \mathit{consumed} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{pending} , \mathit{report} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{wasFailing} , \mathit{told} , \mathit{turn} , \mathit{elapsed} , \mathit{edited} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{touched} , \mathit{own} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - TurnStarts]($heading.id('overwatch---turnstarts'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{TurnStarts} \triangleq \land \mathit{turn} = \texttt{"idle"} \land \mathit{turn} ' = \texttt{"running"} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{toldThisTurn} ' = \mathit{promptQueued} \land \mathit{promptQueued} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{flush} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{truth} , \mathit{head} , \mathit{based} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{from} , \mathit{quiet} , \mathit{installed} , \mathit{produced} , \mathit{consumed} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{pending} , \mathit{report} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{wasFailing} , \mathit{outbox} , \mathit{told} , \mathit{knows} , \mathit{elapsed} , \mathit{edited} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{touched} , \mathit{own} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - WokenTurnStarts]($heading.id('overwatch---wokenturnstarts'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{WokenTurnStarts} \triangleq \mathit{promptQueued} \land \mathit{TurnStarts}
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - TurnCompletes]($heading.id('overwatch---turncompletes'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{TurnCompletes} \triangleq \land \mathit{turn} = \texttt{"running"} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{IF} \mathit{Guard} \\
&\quad \hspace{3.0em}\mathit{THEN} \land \mathit{toldThisTurn} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \land \mathit{knows} ' = \mathit{report} . \mathit{failures} \land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{turn} , \mathit{flush} \rangle \\
&\quad \hspace{3.0em}\mathit{ELSE} \land \mathit{turn} ' = \texttt{"idle"} \land \mathit{flush} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{toldThisTurn} , \mathit{knows} \rangle \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{truth} , \mathit{head} , \mathit{based} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{from} , \mathit{quiet} , \mathit{installed} , \mathit{produced} , \mathit{consumed} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{pending} , \mathit{report} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{wasFailing} , \mathit{outbox} , \mathit{told} , \mathit{promptQueued} , \mathit{elapsed} , \mathit{edited} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{touched} , \mathit{own} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

## [Overwatch - Allowed executions and fairness]($heading.id('overwatch---allowed-executions-and-fairness'))


Next chooses an enabled transition. Spec permits stuttering and requires
weak fairness for the listed progress actions; this does not impose deadlines.

### [Overwatch - Next]($heading.id('overwatch---next'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Next} \triangleq \mathit{Edit} \lor \mathit{OutsideEdit} \lor \mathit{HeadMoves} \lor \mathit{QuietElapses} \lor \mathit{Tick} \lor \mathit{RunEnds} \lor \mathit{TimesOut} \\
&\quad \hspace{2.67em}\lor \mathit{ReadResults} \lor \mathit{Flush} \lor \mathit{TurnStarts} \lor \mathit{TurnCompletes}
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - Spec]($heading.id('overwatch---spec'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Spec} \triangleq \land \mathit{Init} \land \Box [ \mathit{Next} ] _ \mathit{vars} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{WF\_vars} ( \mathit{QuietElapses} ) \land \mathit{WF\_vars} ( \mathit{Tick} ) \land \mathit{WF\_vars} ( \mathit{TimesOut} ) \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{WF\_vars} ( \mathit{ReadResults} ) \land \mathit{WF\_vars} ( \mathit{Flush} ) \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{WF\_vars} ( \mathit{WokenTurnStarts} ) \land \mathit{WF\_vars} ( \mathit{TurnCompletes} )
\end{aligned}
```

## [Overwatch - Safety and progress properties]($heading.id('overwatch---safety-and-progress-properties'))


Results retain their ordering and checked version. The baseline cannot absorb
the session's edits: a non-empty baseline is exactly the failures of a version
at or after the commit that no session edit made or preceded. A failure wakes
the agent only when its read follows the agent's own edit, or when the check
timed out, so another process's changes never wake it. Under Spec fairness,
checks end, and each regression, a failure outside the baseline taken, reaches
the agent or waits, without waking it, for its next turn.
These properties are model-checked within the committed configuration bounds.

### [Overwatch - BufferedResultsAreOrdered]($heading.id('overwatch---bufferedresultsareordered'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{BufferedResultsAreOrdered} \triangleq \land \forall \mathit{i} \in 1 \mathbin{\text{..}} \mathit{Len} ( \mathit{pending} ) : \mathit{pending} [ \mathit{i} ] . \mathit{id} > \mathit{consumed} \land \mathit{pending} [ \mathit{i} ] . \mathit{id} \leq \mathit{produced} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \forall \mathit{i} \in 1 \mathbin{\text{..}} ( \mathit{Len} ( \mathit{pending} ) - 1 ) : \mathit{pending} [ \mathit{i} ] . \mathit{id} < \mathit{pending} [ \mathit{i} + 1 ] . \mathit{id}
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - ReadsSelectLatestComplete]($heading.id('overwatch---readsselectlatestcomplete'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{ReadsSelectLatestComplete} \triangleq \mathit{report} . \mathit{known} \Rightarrow \mathit{report} . \mathit{id} = \mathit{consumed}
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - ResultsMatchBuilds]($heading.id('overwatch---resultsmatchbuilds'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{ResultsMatchBuilds} \triangleq \mathit{report} . \mathit{known} \Rightarrow \mathit{report} . \mathit{failures} = \mathit{truth} [ \mathit{report} . \mathit{at} ] \lor \mathit{report} . \mathit{failures} = \{ \mathit{TimedOut} \}
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - BaselineNeverAbsorbsEdits]($heading.id('overwatch---baselineneverabsorbsedits'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{BaselineNeverAbsorbsEdits} \triangleq \mathit{baseline} . \mathit{known} \Rightarrow \mathit{baseline} . \mathit{failures} = \{ \} \lor \\
&\quad \hspace{2.67em}\land \mathit{baseline} . \mathit{failures} = \mathit{truth} [ \mathit{baseline} . \mathit{at} ] \land \mathit{baseline} . \mathit{at} \geq \mathit{based} \\
&\quad \hspace{2.67em}\land \forall \mathit{w} \in \mathit{own} : \mathit{w} > \mathit{baseline} . \mathit{at}
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - RunsEnd]($heading.id('overwatch---runsend'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{RunsEnd} \triangleq \mathit{busy} \leadsto \neg \mathit{busy}
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - EveryEditIsChecked]($heading.id('overwatch---everyeditischecked'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{EveryEditIsChecked} \triangleq \Diamond \Box ( \mathit{report} . \mathit{known} \land \mathit{report} . \mathit{at} = \mathit{head} )
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - Regressions]($heading.id('overwatch---regressions'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Regressions} \triangleq \mathit{truth} [ \mathit{head} ] \setminus \mathit{IF} \mathit{baseline} . \mathit{known} \mathit{THEN} \mathit{baseline} . \mathit{failures} \mathit{ELSE} \mathit{truth} [ \mathit{based} ]
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - WaitsForTurn]($heading.id('overwatch---waitsforturn'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{WaitsForTurn} \triangleq \mathit{turn} = \texttt{"idle"} \land \mathit{outbox} . \mathit{held} \land \neg \mathit{outbox} . \mathit{waking} \land \mathit{Regressions} \subseteq \mathit{outbox} . \mathit{failures}
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - RegressionsReachAgent]($heading.id('overwatch---regressionsreachagent'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{RegressionsReachAgent} \triangleq \Diamond \Box ( \mathit{Regressions} \subseteq \mathit{knows} \lor \mathit{TimedOut} \in \mathit{knows} \lor \mathit{WaitsForTurn} )
\end{aligned}
```

### [Overwatch - OutsideChangesNeverWake]($heading.id('overwatch---outsidechangesneverwake'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{OutsideChangesNeverWake} \triangleq \Box [ \mathit{told} ' \neq \mathit{told} \land \mathit{told} ' . \mathit{kind} = \texttt{"failed"} \land \mathit{outbox} ' . \mathit{waking} \\
&\quad \hspace{2.67em}\Rightarrow \mathit{edited} \lor \mathit{TimedOut} \in \mathit{outbox} ' . \mathit{failures} ] _ \mathit{vars}
\end{aligned}
```

# [IntegrationContract]($heading.id('integrationcontract'))

[Source](https://github.com/benomahony/overwatch/blob/main/spec/IntegrationContract.tla)

## [IntegrationContract - Imports]($heading.id('integrationcontract---imports'))


Shared operators used by this module are imported below.

### [IntegrationContract - EXTENDS]($heading.id('integrationcontract---extends'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{EXTENDS} \mathit{Naturals} , \mathit{FiniteSets} , \mathit{FailurePolicy}
\end{aligned}
```

## [IntegrationContract - Integration boundary]($heading.id('integrationcontract---integration-boundary'))


This layer receives completed per-check snapshots from Overwatch.
It specifies requests, responses, delivery channels, and session lifecycle
for every host. Both layers use the same FailurePolicy definitions.

### [IntegrationContract - CONSTANTS]($heading.id('integrationcontract---constants'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{CONSTANTS} \mathit{Hosts} , \mathit{Checks} , \mathit{Names} , \mathit{MaxRequests} , \mathit{MaxChanges} , \mathit{MaxSessions}
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - AllHosts]($heading.id('integrationcontract---allhosts'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{AllHosts} \triangleq \{ \texttt{"claude"} , \texttt{"codex"} , \texttt{"opencode1"} , \texttt{"opencode2"} , \texttt{"pi"} , \texttt{"neovim"} \}
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - ASSUME]($heading.id('integrationcontract---assume'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{ASSUME} \mathit{Hosts} \subseteq \mathit{AllHosts} \land \mathit{Hosts} \neq \{ \}
\end{aligned}
```

These are host capabilities, not advisory/strict policy modes. A warning    cannot be counted as a denied completion, and an editor has no agent gate.

## [IntegrationContract - Host capabilities]($heading.id('integrationcontract---host-capabilities'))


The host determines whether protected requests wait for a running check,
how guarded completion is handled, and which delivery channels exist.
A host notices another process's change when it can tell it from the
session's own: Claude Code reads each watcher result against the session's
edits, Codex and OpenCode 2 see a change first at a hook that follows no
edit of the session's, and an editor treats every save alike. Pi and
OpenCode 1 check only after the session's own edits and at settlement, so
they read every result as the session's.
These are integration capabilities, not user-selectable enforcement modes.

### [IntegrationContract - Capabilities]($heading.id('integrationcontract---capabilities'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Capabilities} ( \mathit{h} ) \triangleq [ \mathit{agent} \mapsto \mathit{h} \neq \texttt{"neovim"} , \\
&\quad \hspace{1.67em}\mathit{waitsForCheck} \mapsto \mathit{h} \in \{ \texttt{"codex"} , \texttt{"opencode1"} , \texttt{"opencode2"} , \texttt{"pi"} \} , \\
&\quad \hspace{1.67em}\mathit{completion} \mapsto \mathit{CASE} \mathit{h} \in \{ \texttt{"claude"} , \texttt{"codex"} \} \to \texttt{"block"} \\
&\quad \hspace{7.33em}\Box \mathit{h} = \texttt{"opencode1"} \to \texttt{"warn"} \\
&\quad \hspace{7.33em}\Box \mathit{h} = \texttt{"opencode2"} \to \texttt{"queue"} \\
&\quad \hspace{7.33em}\Box \mathit{h} = \texttt{"pi"} \to \texttt{"continue"} \\
&\quad \hspace{7.33em}\Box \mathit{OTHER} \to \texttt{"none"} , \\
&\quad \hspace{1.67em}\mathit{delivery} \mapsto \mathit{CASE} \mathit{h} = \texttt{"claude"} \to \texttt{"turn"} \\
&\quad \hspace{6.67em}\Box \mathit{h} = \texttt{"opencode2"} \to \texttt{"context"} \\
&\quad \hspace{6.67em}\Box \mathit{h} = \texttt{"neovim"} \to \texttt{"quickfix"} \\
&\quad \hspace{6.67em}\Box \mathit{OTHER} \to \texttt{"event"} , \\
&\quad \hspace{1.67em}\mathit{idleWake} \mapsto \mathit{h} \in \{ \texttt{"claude"} , \texttt{"opencode2"} \} , \\
&\quad \hspace{1.67em}\mathit{status} \mapsto \mathit{h} \in \{ \texttt{"claude"} , \texttt{"pi"} , \texttt{"neovim"} \} , \\
&\quad \hspace{1.67em}\mathit{noticesOutside} \mapsto \mathit{h} \in \{ \texttt{"claude"} , \texttt{"codex"} , \texttt{"opencode2"} , \texttt{"neovim"} \} ]
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - Kinds]($heading.id('integrationcontract---kinds'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Kinds} \triangleq \{ \texttt{"inspect"} , \texttt{"repair"} , \texttt{"publish"} , \texttt{"complete"} \}
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - Empty]($heading.id('integrationcontract---empty'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Empty} \triangleq [ \mathit{c} \in \mathit{Checks} \mapsto \{ \} ]
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - Snapshots]($heading.id('integrationcontract---snapshots'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Snapshots} \triangleq [ \mathit{Checks} \to \mathit{SUBSET} \mathit{Names} ]
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - NoReply]($heading.id('integrationcontract---noreply'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{NoReply} \triangleq [ \mathit{ready} \mapsto \mathit{FALSE} , \mathit{decision} \mapsto \texttt{"none"} ]
\end{aligned}
```

## [IntegrationContract - State shape]($heading.id('integrationcontract---state-shape'))


Request and reply are separate so that a check can finish or a session can
close between them. Report visibility, deferred context, corrections, and
idle wakeups are separate observations.

### [IntegrationContract - VARIABLES]($heading.id('integrationcontract---variables'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{VARIABLES} \mathit{host} , \mathit{active} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{reports} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{inherited} , \mathit{selected} , \\
&\quad \hspace{3.33em}\mathit{request} , \mathit{reply} , \mathit{requests} , \mathit{changes} , \mathit{session} , \\
&\quad \hspace{3.33em}\mathit{visible} , \mathit{contextPending} , \mathit{contextSent} , \mathit{correctionQueued} , \\
&\quad \hspace{3.33em}\mathit{contexts} , \mathit{warnings} , \mathit{corrections} , \mathit{inTurn} , \mathit{wakes} , \mathit{work} , \\
&\quad \hspace{3.33em}\mathit{correctionPending} , \mathit{correctionTurn} , \mathit{outside} , \mathit{outsides}
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - vars]($heading.id('integrationcontract---vars'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{vars} \triangleq \langle \mathit{host} , \mathit{active} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{reports} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{inherited} , \mathit{selected} , \\
&\quad \hspace{3.33em}\mathit{request} , \mathit{reply} , \mathit{requests} , \mathit{changes} , \mathit{session} , \mathit{visible} , \\
&\quad \hspace{3.33em}\mathit{contextPending} , \mathit{contextSent} , \mathit{correctionQueued} , \mathit{contexts} , \\
&\quad \hspace{3.33em}\mathit{warnings} , \mathit{corrections} , \mathit{inTurn} , \mathit{wakes} , \mathit{work} , \\
&\quad \hspace{3.33em}\mathit{correctionPending} , \mathit{correctionTurn} , \mathit{outside} , \mathit{outsides} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

## [IntegrationContract - Guard selection and inherited policy]($heading.id('integrationcontract---guard-selection-and-inherited-policy'))


An empty selection means all checks. FailureGuards decides whether each
selected check guards publication; Notify identifies new failures for delivery.

### [IntegrationContract - Guarded]($heading.id('integrationcontract---guarded'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Guarded} ( \mathit{scope} ) \triangleq \{ \mathit{c} \in \mathit{scope} : \mathit{FailureGuards} ( \mathit{reports} [ \mathit{c} ] , \mathit{baseline} [ \mathit{c} ] , \mathit{inherited} ) \}
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - Guard]($heading.id('integrationcontract---guard'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Guard} \triangleq \mathit{Capabilities} ( \mathit{host} ) . \mathit{agent} \land \mathit{Guarded} ( \mathit{Checks} ) \neq \{ \}
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - Notify]($heading.id('integrationcontract---notify'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Notify} \triangleq \mathit{Capabilities} ( \mathit{host} ) . \mathit{agent} \land \\
&\quad \hspace{3.33em}( \exists \mathit{c} \in \mathit{Checks} : \mathit{FailureGuards} ( \mathit{reports} [ \mathit{c} ] , \mathit{baseline} [ \mathit{c} ] , \texttt{"allow"} ) )
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - SelectedChecks]($heading.id('integrationcontract---selectedchecks'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{SelectedChecks} \triangleq \mathit{IF} \mathit{selected} = \{ \} \mathit{THEN} \mathit{Checks} \mathit{ELSE} \mathit{selected}
\end{aligned}
```

## [IntegrationContract - State domains]($heading.id('integrationcontract---state-domains'))


Counters and snapshots are bounded for TLC exploration. These bounds
do not assert a runtime limit on requests or sessions.

### [IntegrationContract - TypeOK]($heading.id('integrationcontract---typeok'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{TypeOK} \triangleq \land \mathit{host} \in \mathit{Hosts} \land \mathit{active} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \land \mathit{busy} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{work} \in 0 \mathbin{\text{..}} ( ( \mathit{MaxSessions} + 1 ) * \mathit{MaxRequests} ) \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{inTurn} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{wakes} \in 0 \mathbin{\text{..}} ( \mathit{MaxChanges} + \mathit{MaxSessions} + 1 + ( \mathit{MaxSessions} + 1 ) * \mathit{MaxRequests} ) \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{reports} \in \mathit{Snapshots} \land \mathit{baseline} \in \mathit{Snapshots} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{inherited} \in \{ \texttt{"allow"} , \texttt{"block"} \} \land \mathit{selected} \subseteq \mathit{Checks} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{request} \in \mathit{Kinds} \cup \{ \texttt{"none"} \} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{reply} \in [ \mathit{ready} : \mathit{BOOLEAN} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{decision} : \{ \texttt{"none"} , \texttt{"allow"} , \texttt{"deny"} , \texttt{"block"} , \texttt{"warn"} , \texttt{"queue"} , \texttt{"continue"} , \texttt{"cancelled"} \} ] \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{requests} \in 0 \mathbin{\text{..}} \mathit{MaxRequests} \land \mathit{changes} \in 0 \mathbin{\text{..}} \mathit{MaxChanges} \land \mathit{session} \in 0 \mathbin{\text{..}} \mathit{MaxSessions} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{visible} \in [ \mathit{known} : \mathit{BOOLEAN} , \mathit{failures} : \mathit{Snapshots} ] \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{contextPending} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \land \mathit{contextSent} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \land \mathit{correctionQueued} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{contexts} \in 0 \mathbin{\text{..}} ( \mathit{MaxChanges} + \mathit{MaxSessions} + 1 ) \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{warnings} \in 0 \mathbin{\text{..}} ( ( \mathit{MaxSessions} + 1 ) * \mathit{MaxRequests} ) \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{corrections} \in 0 \mathbin{\text{..}} ( ( \mathit{MaxSessions} + 1 ) * \mathit{MaxRequests} ) \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{correctionPending} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \land \mathit{correctionTurn} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \land \mathit{outside} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{outsides} \in 0 \mathbin{\text{..}} \mathit{MaxChanges}
\end{aligned}
```

## [IntegrationContract - Initial state]($heading.id('integrationcontract---initial-state'))


A host starts active with arbitrary reports, baseline, policy, and check state.
No reply, visible report, deferred context, or correction has been produced.

### [IntegrationContract - Init]($heading.id('integrationcontract---init'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Init} \triangleq \land \mathit{host} \in \mathit{Hosts} \land \mathit{active} = \mathit{TRUE} \land \mathit{busy} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{reports} \in \mathit{Snapshots} \land \mathit{baseline} \in \mathit{Snapshots} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{inherited} \in \{ \texttt{"allow"} , \texttt{"block"} \} \land \mathit{selected} \in \mathit{SUBSET} \mathit{Checks} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{request} = \texttt{"none"} \land \mathit{reply} = \mathit{NoReply} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{requests} = 0 \land \mathit{changes} = 0 \land \mathit{session} = 0 \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{visible} = [ \mathit{known} \mapsto \mathit{FALSE} , \mathit{failures} \mapsto \mathit{Empty} ] \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{contextPending} = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{contextSent} = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{correctionQueued} = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{contexts} = 0 \land \mathit{warnings} = 0 \land \mathit{corrections} = 0 \land \mathit{wakes} = 0 \land \mathit{work} = 0 \land \mathit{inTurn} \in \mathit{BOOLEAN} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{correctionPending} = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{correctionTurn} = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{outside} = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{outsides} = 0
\end{aligned}
```

## [IntegrationContract - Requests and completion decisions]($heading.id('integrationcontract---requests-and-completion-decisions'))


Inspection and repair remain answerable during checks. Protected requests
follow the host waiting capability and consult the selected reports.
Respond records the decision and accounts separately for warnings,
corrections, and wakeups; Acknowledge releases the request slot.

### [IntegrationContract - Request]($heading.id('integrationcontract---request'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Request} ( \mathit{k} ) \triangleq \land \mathit{active} \land \mathit{request} = \texttt{"none"} \land \mathit{requests} < \mathit{MaxRequests} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{request} ' = \mathit{k} \land \mathit{reply} ' = \mathit{NoReply} \land \mathit{requests} ' = \mathit{requests} + 1 \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{host} , \mathit{active} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{reports} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{inherited} , \mathit{selected} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{changes} , \mathit{session} , \mathit{visible} , \mathit{contextPending} , \mathit{contextSent} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{correctionQueued} , \mathit{contexts} , \mathit{warnings} , \mathit{corrections} , \mathit{inTurn} , \mathit{wakes} , \mathit{work} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{correctionPending} , \mathit{correctionTurn} , \mathit{outside} , \mathit{outsides} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - CanRespond]($heading.id('integrationcontract---canrespond'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{CanRespond} \triangleq \mathit{active} \land \mathit{request} \neq \texttt{"none"} \land \neg \mathit{reply} . \mathit{ready} \land \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}( \mathit{request} \in \{ \texttt{"inspect"} , \texttt{"repair"} \} \lor \neg \mathit{Capabilities} ( \mathit{host} ) . \mathit{agent} \lor \\
&\quad \hspace{1.67em}\neg \mathit{Capabilities} ( \mathit{host} ) . \mathit{waitsForCheck} \lor \neg \mathit{busy} )
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - Decision]($heading.id('integrationcontract---decision'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Decision} \triangleq \mathit{CASE} \mathit{request} \in \{ \texttt{"inspect"} , \texttt{"repair"} \} \to \texttt{"allow"} \\
&\quad \hspace{2.0em}\Box \mathit{request} = \texttt{"publish"} \to \\
&\quad \hspace{3.67em}\mathit{IF} \mathit{Capabilities} ( \mathit{host} ) . \mathit{agent} \land \mathit{Guarded} ( \mathit{SelectedChecks} ) \neq \{ \} \\
&\quad \hspace{3.67em}\mathit{THEN} \texttt{"deny"} \mathit{ELSE} \texttt{"allow"} \\
&\quad \hspace{2.0em}\Box \mathit{request} = \texttt{"complete"} \to \mathit{IF} \mathit{Guard} \mathit{THEN} \mathit{Capabilities} ( \mathit{host} ) . \mathit{completion} \mathit{ELSE} \texttt{"allow"}
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - QueuesCorrection]($heading.id('integrationcontract---queuescorrection'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{QueuesCorrection} \triangleq \mathit{Decision} = \texttt{"queue"} \lor ( \mathit{host} = \texttt{"claude"} \land \mathit{Decision} = \texttt{"block"} )
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - EndsTurn]($heading.id('integrationcontract---endsturn'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{EndsTurn} \triangleq \mathit{request} = \texttt{"complete"} \land ( \mathit{Decision} \in \{ \texttt{"allow"} , \texttt{"warn"} , \texttt{"queue"} \} \lor \mathit{host} = \texttt{"claude"} )
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - Respond]($heading.id('integrationcontract---respond'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Respond} \triangleq \land \mathit{CanRespond} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{inTurn} ' = \mathit{IF} \mathit{EndsTurn} \mathit{THEN} \mathit{FALSE} \mathit{ELSE} \mathit{inTurn} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{correctionTurn} ' = \mathit{IF} \mathit{EndsTurn} \mathit{THEN} \mathit{FALSE} \mathit{ELSE} \mathit{correctionTurn} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{correctionPending} ' = ( \mathit{correctionPending} \lor ( \mathit{QueuesCorrection} \land \neg \mathit{correctionQueued} ) ) \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{reply} ' = [ \mathit{ready} \mapsto \mathit{TRUE} , \mathit{decision} \mapsto \mathit{Decision} ] \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{warnings} ' = \mathit{warnings} + \mathit{IF} \mathit{Decision} = \texttt{"warn"} \mathit{THEN} 1 \mathit{ELSE} 0 \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{corrections} ' = \mathit{corrections} + \mathit{IF} \mathit{QueuesCorrection} \land \neg \mathit{correctionQueued} \mathit{THEN} 1 \mathit{ELSE} 0 \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{correctionQueued} ' = ( \mathit{correctionQueued} \lor \mathit{QueuesCorrection} ) \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{wakes} ' = \mathit{wakes} + \mathit{IF} \mathit{QueuesCorrection} \land \neg \mathit{correctionQueued} \land \\
&\quad \hspace{9.33em}( \mathit{host} = \texttt{"opencode2"} \lor \neg \mathit{inTurn} ) \\
&\quad \hspace{8.33em}\mathit{THEN} 1 \mathit{ELSE} 0 \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{host} , \mathit{active} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{reports} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{inherited} , \mathit{selected} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{request} , \mathit{requests} , \mathit{changes} , \mathit{session} , \mathit{visible} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{contextPending} , \mathit{contextSent} , \mathit{contexts} , \mathit{work} , \mathit{outside} , \mathit{outsides} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - Acknowledge]($heading.id('integrationcontract---acknowledge'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Acknowledge} \triangleq \land \mathit{request} \neq \texttt{"none"} \land \mathit{reply} . \mathit{ready} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{request} ' = \texttt{"none"} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{host} , \mathit{active} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{reports} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{inherited} , \mathit{selected} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{reply} , \mathit{requests} , \mathit{changes} , \mathit{session} , \mathit{visible} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{contextPending} , \mathit{contextSent} , \mathit{correctionQueued} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{contexts} , \mathit{warnings} , \mathit{corrections} , \mathit{inTurn} , \mathit{wakes} , \mathit{work} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{correctionPending} , \mathit{correctionTurn} , \mathit{outside} , \mathit{outsides} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

## [IntegrationContract - Checks and result delivery]($heading.id('integrationcontract---checks-and-result-delivery'))


A completed check replaces the reports. Changed findings invalidate old
delivery and correction deduplication. Report updates visibility and either
publishes event context or retains it for Deliver. Recovery clears stale context.

### [IntegrationContract - BeginCheck]($heading.id('integrationcontract---begincheck'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{BeginCheck} \triangleq \land \mathit{active} \land \neg \mathit{busy} \land \mathit{changes} < \mathit{MaxChanges} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{busy} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{host} , \mathit{active} , \mathit{reports} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{inherited} , \mathit{selected} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{request} , \mathit{reply} , \mathit{requests} , \mathit{changes} , \mathit{session} , \mathit{visible} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{contextPending} , \mathit{contextSent} , \mathit{correctionQueued} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{contexts} , \mathit{warnings} , \mathit{corrections} , \mathit{inTurn} , \mathit{wakes} , \mathit{work} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{correctionPending} , \mathit{correctionTurn} , \mathit{outside} , \mathit{outsides} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

The result-ordering and baseline rules are specified in Overwatch.tla.    This layer accepts a completed result at that boundary, then constrains    what every host must expose and which requests it may hold behind a check.

### [IntegrationContract - FinishCheck]($heading.id('integrationcontract---finishcheck'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{FinishCheck} ( \mathit{f} ) \triangleq \land \mathit{active} \land \mathit{busy} \land \mathit{changes} < \mathit{MaxChanges} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{reports} ' = \mathit{f} \land \mathit{busy} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{changes} ' = \mathit{changes} + 1 \land \mathit{outside} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{IF} \mathit{f} \neq \mathit{reports} \\
&\quad \hspace{3.0em}\mathit{THEN} \land \mathit{contextSent} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{correctionQueued} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{4.67em}\land \mathit{contextPending} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{3.0em}\mathit{ELSE} \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{contextSent} , \mathit{correctionQueued} , \mathit{contextPending} \rangle \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{host} , \mathit{active} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{inherited} , \mathit{selected} , \mathit{request} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{reply} , \mathit{requests} , \mathit{session} , \mathit{visible} , \mathit{contexts} , \mathit{warnings} , \mathit{corrections} , \mathit{inTurn} , \mathit{wakes} , \mathit{work} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{correctionPending} , \mathit{correctionTurn} , \mathit{outsides} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

A check that finishes on another process's change, with no session edit    since the last result, replaces the reports for status and guards alone:    it neither releases correction deduplication nor counts as a change the    session made, and Report gives it no failure context. A context still    waiting for the old reports is dropped, as a newer result replaces it.

### [IntegrationContract - OutsideFinish]($heading.id('integrationcontract---outsidefinish'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{OutsideFinish} ( \mathit{f} ) \triangleq \land \mathit{active} \land \mathit{busy} \land \mathit{outsides} < \mathit{MaxChanges} \land \mathit{Capabilities} ( \mathit{host} ) . \mathit{noticesOutside} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{reports} ' = \mathit{f} \land \mathit{busy} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{outside} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \land \mathit{outsides} ' = \mathit{outsides} + 1 \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{contextPending} ' = ( \mathit{contextPending} \land \mathit{f} = \mathit{reports} ) \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{host} , \mathit{active} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{inherited} , \mathit{selected} , \mathit{request} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{reply} , \mathit{requests} , \mathit{changes} , \mathit{session} , \mathit{visible} , \mathit{contextSent} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{correctionQueued} , \mathit{contexts} , \mathit{warnings} , \mathit{corrections} , \mathit{inTurn} , \mathit{wakes} , \mathit{work} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{correctionPending} , \mathit{correctionTurn} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - Told]($heading.id('integrationcontract---told'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Told} \triangleq \mathit{Notify} \land \neg \mathit{outside}
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - Report]($heading.id('integrationcontract---report'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Report} \triangleq \land \mathit{active} \land \neg \mathit{busy} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{visible} ' = [ \mathit{known} \mapsto \mathit{TRUE} , \mathit{failures} \mapsto \mathit{reports} ] \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{contextPending} ' = ( \mathit{Told} \land \neg \mathit{contextSent} \land \mathit{Capabilities} ( \mathit{host} ) . \mathit{delivery} \in \{ \texttt{"turn"} , \texttt{"context"} \} ) \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{contextSent} ' = ( \mathit{contextSent} \lor ( \mathit{Told} \land \mathit{Capabilities} ( \mathit{host} ) . \mathit{delivery} = \texttt{"event"} ) ) \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{contexts} ' = \mathit{contexts} + \mathit{IF} \mathit{Told} \land \neg \mathit{contextSent} \land \mathit{Capabilities} ( \mathit{host} ) . \mathit{delivery} = \texttt{"event"} \mathit{THEN} 1 \mathit{ELSE} 0 \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{host} , \mathit{active} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{reports} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{inherited} , \mathit{selected} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{request} , \mathit{reply} , \mathit{requests} , \mathit{changes} , \mathit{session} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{correctionQueued} , \mathit{warnings} , \mathit{corrections} , \mathit{inTurn} , \mathit{wakes} , \mathit{work} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{correctionPending} , \mathit{correctionTurn} , \mathit{outside} , \mathit{outsides} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - Deliver]($heading.id('integrationcontract---deliver'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Deliver} \triangleq \land \mathit{active} \land \mathit{contextPending} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{wakes} ' = \mathit{wakes} + \mathit{IF} \mathit{host} = \texttt{"claude"} \land \neg \mathit{inTurn} \mathit{THEN} 1 \mathit{ELSE} 0 \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{contextSent} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \land \mathit{contextPending} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{contexts} ' = \mathit{contexts} + 1 \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{host} , \mathit{active} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{reports} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{inherited} , \mathit{selected} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{request} , \mathit{reply} , \mathit{requests} , \mathit{changes} , \mathit{session} , \mathit{visible} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{correctionQueued} , \mathit{warnings} , \mathit{corrections} , \mathit{inTurn} , \mathit{work} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{correctionPending} , \mathit{correctionTurn} , \mathit{outside} , \mathit{outsides} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

## [IntegrationContract - Shutdown restart and new work]($heading.id('integrationcontract---shutdown-restart-and-new-work'))


Stop cancels an outstanding request and clears visible and pending delivery.
Restart preserves project policy, takes reports as the new baseline, and
resets delivery state. A submitted correction runs in a turn of its own,
which on OpenCode 2 is always the next; any other turn is the person's.
Completed tool work permits a fresh correction, except in the correction's
own turn, where inspecting and repairing are its answer.

### [IntegrationContract - Stop]($heading.id('integrationcontract---stop'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Stop} \triangleq \land \mathit{active} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{inTurn} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{correctionPending} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{correctionTurn} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{active} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{busy} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{request} ' = \texttt{"none"} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{reply} ' = [ \mathit{ready} \mapsto \mathit{TRUE} , \mathit{decision} \mapsto \texttt{"cancelled"} ] \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{visible} ' = [ \mathit{known} \mapsto \mathit{FALSE} , \mathit{failures} \mapsto \mathit{Empty} ] \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{contextPending} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{host} , \mathit{reports} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{inherited} , \mathit{selected} , \mathit{requests} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{changes} , \mathit{session} , \mathit{contextSent} , \mathit{correctionQueued} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{contexts} , \mathit{warnings} , \mathit{corrections} , \mathit{wakes} , \mathit{work} , \mathit{outside} , \mathit{outsides} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - Restart]($heading.id('integrationcontract---restart'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Restart} \triangleq \land \neg \mathit{active} \land \mathit{session} < \mathit{MaxSessions} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{inTurn} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{correctionPending} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{correctionTurn} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{active} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \land \mathit{session} ' = \mathit{session} + 1 \land \mathit{busy} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{baseline} ' = \mathit{reports} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{request} ' = \texttt{"none"} \land \mathit{reply} ' = \mathit{NoReply} \land \mathit{requests} ' = 0 \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{visible} ' = [ \mathit{known} \mapsto \mathit{FALSE} , \mathit{failures} \mapsto \mathit{Empty} ] \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{contextPending} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{contextSent} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{correctionQueued} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \land \mathit{outside} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{host} , \mathit{reports} , \mathit{inherited} , \mathit{selected} , \mathit{changes} , \mathit{contexts} , \mathit{warnings} , \mathit{corrections} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{wakes} , \mathit{work} , \mathit{outsides} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - StartTurn]($heading.id('integrationcontract---startturn'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{StartTurn} \triangleq \land \mathit{active} \land \neg \mathit{inTurn} \land \mathit{inTurn} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \neg ( \mathit{host} = \texttt{"opencode2"} \land \mathit{correctionPending} ) \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{correctionTurn} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{host} , \mathit{active} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{reports} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{inherited} , \mathit{selected} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{request} , \mathit{reply} , \mathit{requests} , \mathit{changes} , \mathit{session} , \mathit{visible} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{contextPending} , \mathit{contextSent} , \mathit{correctionQueued} , \mathit{contexts} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{warnings} , \mathit{corrections} , \mathit{wakes} , \mathit{work} , \mathit{correctionPending} , \mathit{outside} , \mathit{outsides} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - StartCorrectionTurn]($heading.id('integrationcontract---startcorrectionturn'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{StartCorrectionTurn} \triangleq \land \mathit{active} \land \neg \mathit{inTurn} \land \mathit{correctionPending} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{inTurn} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \land \mathit{correctionTurn} ' = \mathit{TRUE} \land \mathit{correctionPending} ' = \mathit{FALSE} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{host} , \mathit{active} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{reports} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{inherited} , \mathit{selected} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{request} , \mathit{reply} , \mathit{requests} , \mathit{changes} , \mathit{session} , \mathit{visible} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{contextPending} , \mathit{contextSent} , \mathit{correctionQueued} , \mathit{contexts} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{warnings} , \mathit{corrections} , \mathit{wakes} , \mathit{work} , \mathit{outside} , \mathit{outsides} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - WorkCompleted]($heading.id('integrationcontract---workcompleted'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{WorkCompleted} \triangleq \land \mathit{active} \land \mathit{work} < ( \mathit{MaxSessions} + 1 ) * \mathit{MaxRequests} \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{work} ' = \mathit{work} + \mathit{IF} \mathit{correctionTurn} \mathit{THEN} 0 \mathit{ELSE} 1 \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{correctionQueued} ' = ( \mathit{correctionTurn} \land \mathit{correctionQueued} ) \\
&\quad \hspace{1.33em}\land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \langle \mathit{host} , \mathit{active} , \mathit{busy} , \mathit{reports} , \mathit{baseline} , \mathit{inherited} , \mathit{selected} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{request} , \mathit{reply} , \mathit{requests} , \mathit{changes} , \mathit{session} , \mathit{visible} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{contextPending} , \mathit{contextSent} , \mathit{contexts} , \mathit{warnings} , \mathit{corrections} , \mathit{inTurn} , \mathit{wakes} , \\
&\quad \hspace{6.33em}\mathit{correctionPending} , \mathit{correctionTurn} , \mathit{outside} , \mathit{outsides} \rangle
\end{aligned}
```

## [IntegrationContract - Allowed executions and fairness]($heading.id('integrationcontract---allowed-executions-and-fairness'))


Spec composes check-completion fairness with fair response and report
servicing. Inspection independence is a safety property: its response
remains enabled even while a check is held.

### [IntegrationContract - CheckCompletes]($heading.id('integrationcontract---checkcompletes'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{CheckCompletes} \triangleq \exists \mathit{f} \in \mathit{Snapshots} : \mathit{FinishCheck} ( \mathit{f} ) \lor \mathit{OutsideFinish} ( \mathit{f} )
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - Next]($heading.id('integrationcontract---next'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Next} \triangleq ( \exists \mathit{k} \in \mathit{Kinds} : \mathit{Request} ( \mathit{k} ) ) \lor \mathit{Respond} \lor \mathit{Acknowledge} \lor \mathit{BeginCheck} \\
&\quad \hspace{2.67em}\lor \mathit{CheckCompletes} \lor \mathit{Report} \lor \mathit{Deliver} \lor \mathit{Stop} \lor \mathit{Restart} \\
&\quad \hspace{2.67em}\lor \mathit{StartTurn} \lor \mathit{StartCorrectionTurn} \lor \mathit{WorkCompleted} \\
&\quad \hspace{2.67em}\lor ( \neg \mathit{active} \land \mathit{session} = \mathit{MaxSessions} \land \mathit{UNCHANGED} \mathit{vars} )
\end{aligned}
```

Check completion fairness is the RunsEnd guarantee of the result model.    Inspection is independently enabled; it never needs that guarantee to reply.

### [IntegrationContract - Spec]($heading.id('integrationcontract---spec'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{Spec} \triangleq \mathit{Init} \land \Box [ \mathit{Next} ] _ \mathit{vars} \land \mathit{WF\_vars} ( \mathit{CheckCompletes} ) \\
&\quad \hspace{2.67em}\land \mathit{WF\_vars} ( \mathit{Respond} ) \land \mathit{WF\_vars} ( \mathit{Report} ) \land \mathit{WF\_vars} ( \mathit{Deliver} )
\end{aligned}
```

## [IntegrationContract - Safety and progress properties]($heading.id('integrationcontract---safety-and-progress-properties'))


Capabilities constrain completion, editors never acquire agent gates,
closed sessions stay silent, pending context stays current, and corrections
are deduplicated. Progress properties require the fairness stated in Spec.

### [IntegrationContract - InspectionIndependentOfChecks]($heading.id('integrationcontract---inspectionindependentofchecks'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{InspectionIndependentOfChecks} \triangleq \mathit{active} \land \mathit{request} \in \{ \texttt{"inspect"} , \texttt{"repair"} \} \land \neg \mathit{reply} . \mathit{ready} \Rightarrow \mathit{ENABLED} \mathit{Respond}
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - InspectionAlwaysAllowed]($heading.id('integrationcontract---inspectionalwaysallowed'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{InspectionAlwaysAllowed} \triangleq \mathit{request} \in \{ \texttt{"inspect"} , \texttt{"repair"} \} \land \mathit{reply} . \mathit{ready} \Rightarrow \mathit{reply} . \mathit{decision} = \texttt{"allow"}
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - EditorNeverGuards]($heading.id('integrationcontract---editorneverguards'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{EditorNeverGuards} \triangleq \mathit{host} = \texttt{"neovim"} \land \mathit{request} \neq \texttt{"none"} \land \mathit{reply} . \mathit{ready} \Rightarrow \mathit{reply} . \mathit{decision} = \texttt{"allow"}
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - StoppedSessionsStaySilent]($heading.id('integrationcontract---stoppedsessionsstaysilent'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{StoppedSessionsStaySilent} \triangleq \neg \mathit{active} \Rightarrow \neg \mathit{contextPending} \land \neg \mathit{visible} . \mathit{known}
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - HostsWithoutIdleWakeStayIdle]($heading.id('integrationcontract---hostswithoutidlewakestayidle'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{HostsWithoutIdleWakeStayIdle} \triangleq \neg \mathit{Capabilities} ( \mathit{host} ) . \mathit{idleWake} \Rightarrow \mathit{wakes} = 0
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - CorrectionRequestsAreDeduplicated]($heading.id('integrationcontract---correctionrequestsarededuplicated'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{CorrectionRequestsAreDeduplicated} \triangleq \mathit{corrections} \leq \mathit{changes} + \mathit{session} + \mathit{work} + 1
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - PendingContextIsCurrent]($heading.id('integrationcontract---pendingcontextiscurrent'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{PendingContextIsCurrent} \triangleq \mathit{contextPending} \Rightarrow \mathit{Notify}
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - CompletionUsesHostCapability]($heading.id('integrationcontract---completionuseshostcapability'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{CompletionUsesHostCapability} \triangleq \mathit{request} = \texttt{"complete"} \land \mathit{reply} . \mathit{ready} \Rightarrow \\
&\quad \hspace{2.33em}\mathit{reply} . \mathit{decision} \in \{ \texttt{"allow"} , \mathit{Capabilities} ( \mathit{host} ) . \mathit{completion} \}
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - EditorOnlyReports]($heading.id('integrationcontract---editoronlyreports'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{EditorOnlyReports} \triangleq \mathit{host} = \texttt{"neovim"} \Rightarrow \mathit{contexts} = 0 \land \mathit{warnings} = 0 \land \mathit{corrections} = 0 \land \mathit{wakes} = 0
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - PendingReportsEventuallyResolve]($heading.id('integrationcontract---pendingreportseventuallyresolve'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{PendingReportsEventuallyResolve} \triangleq \mathit{contextPending} \leadsto \neg \mathit{contextPending}
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - FinishedReportsBecomeVisible]($heading.id('integrationcontract---finishedreportsbecomevisible'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{FinishedReportsBecomeVisible} \triangleq ( \mathit{active} \land \neg \mathit{busy} ) \leadsto ( \mathit{visible} . \mathit{known} \lor \neg \mathit{active} )
\end{aligned}
```

### [IntegrationContract - InspectionEventuallyReplies]($heading.id('integrationcontract---inspectioneventuallyreplies'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{InspectionEventuallyReplies} \triangleq ( \mathit{active} \land \mathit{request} \in \{ \texttt{"inspect"} , \texttt{"repair"} \} \land \neg \mathit{reply} . \mathit{ready} ) \\
&\quad \hspace{2.0em}\leadsto ( \mathit{reply} . \mathit{ready} \lor \neg \mathit{active} )
\end{aligned}
```

# [IntegrationLifecycle]($heading.id('integrationlifecycle'))

[Source](https://github.com/benomahony/overwatch/blob/main/spec/IntegrationLifecycle.tla)

## [IntegrationLifecycle - Lifecycle instance]($heading.id('integrationlifecycle---lifecycle-instance'))


This module reuses the complete IntegrationContract specification.
Its TLC configuration explores shutdown and restart with a separate bound.

### [IntegrationLifecycle - EXTENDS]($heading.id('integrationlifecycle---extends'))

```=mathtex
\begin{aligned}
&\mathit{EXTENDS} \mathit{IntegrationContract}
\end{aligned}
```


